Package: microclimf
Type: Package
Title: Fast above, below or within canopy gridded microclimate modelling with R
Version: 3.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ilya", "Maclean", email = "i.m.d.maclean@exeter.ac.uk", role = "cre"))
Maintainer: Ilya M. D. Maclean <i.m.d.maclean@exeter.ac.uk>
Description: Provides a mechanistic model of microclimate above, within and below
    vegetation canopies and below ground. The model predicts gridded hourly temperature,
    humidity, wind speed, radiation and soil moisture across real landscapes from standard
    weather data, elevation, vegetation and soil properties. Canopy and ground energy
    balance are coupled to multilayer soil heat and water, two-stream radiation and
    stomatal conductance. To make landscape-scale simulations computationally efficient,
    the full iterative energy-balance model is solved at one representative location, and
    conditions in surrounding grid cells are then calculated from that solution while
    accounting for local terrain, shading, vegetation and soil differences. The full model
    can alternatively be run independently for every grid cell, with support for tiled and
    parallel processing. Additional functions calculate microclimate equivalents of the 19
    standard bioclimatic variables. Core computations are implemented in C++. Snow is not
    currently represented.
